  "id": "COMPOUND:29863 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism linking (+)-Iridodial lactol to VMRC-LCP through a series of target interactions. The drug is implicated in targeting two distinct proteins: 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 and Ataxin-2, both of which are targets of other compounds (WS-5995 B and Diplotrin A, respectively). These targets ultimately converge on VMRC-LCP, indicating a possible pathway where (+)-Iridodial lactol may modulate the activity of these proteins, which in turn influence VMRC-LCP. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on VMRC-LCP supports the hypothesis that (+)-Iridodial lactol may act through a regulatory or inhibitory pathway involving these proteins. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the precise role of (+)-Iridodial lactol in this process.",
